-- Migration 1915 — withdraw 206 stance chairs that were seated on an ABSENCE of evidence.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS. The absence detector, run corpus-wide on 2026-10-09 over all 38,405 context rows
-- carrying reasoning, produced a tier-A queue: rows whose reasoning states its own absence of
-- evidence ("no documented position", "no record of", "no evidence he…") AND which carry no
-- quotation, no instrument and no rung-contrast beside it. 317 of those are voter-facing. Every
-- one of the 307 actionable rows was then READ BY HAND, one at a time, and recorded with a reason
-- in C:/ev-stance-work/absence/LEDGER.md. 206 failed; 101 passed and are untouched; 10 are blocked
-- because `immigration` is the only live topic with no Season 2 ladder to write to.
--
-- ⚖ WHAT A BLANK HERE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It asserts that the row's own reasoning does
-- not support the chair it carries. It does NOT assert the person holds no view. Each row records
-- which kind of nothing it is, in its own INTERNAL RECORD prose.
--
-- 🔑 WHY A SEASON 2 BLANK AND NOT A SEASON 1 EDIT. Season 1 is closed and immutable. Verified in
-- backend/src/lib/compassService.ts before writing: a Season 2 answer of 0 SUPPRESSES the pair —
-- `NULLIF(pa.value, 0) AS stance_value`, with the guard deliberately OUTSIDE the season collapse,
-- "a blank in the newest season suppresses the answer, it does not fall through to the previous
-- season's rung" (seasonCompositionService.ts). So writing 0 here withdraws the Season 1 row from
-- every serving path without rewriting a closed season.
--
-- 🔑 THE CARRY QUESTION DOES NOT ARISE, AND THAT WAS CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. `cs` resolves the
-- displayed rung text from `pa.topic_revision_id` — the ANSWER'S OWN revision — so a Season 1 answer
-- is shown with Season 1 rung text and Season 1 reasoning. These rows are internally coherent; they
-- are not mislabelled by the Season 2 ladder, and nothing here is re-seated onto it. The per-topic
-- carry analysis (24 rungs where Season 2 asks a genuinely different question) is recorded in
-- C:/ev-stance-work/absence/carry_rulings.py for the next pass that DOES repair forward.
--
-- COMPOSITION. 206 rows across 153 people. 189 are Season 1 pairs with no Season 2 answer, so they
-- INSERT. 17 are Season 2 rows where the defective answer IS the Season 2 answer, so they UPDATE.
-- One statement does both: (politician_id, topic_id, season_id) is the PK on BOTH tables.
--
-- THE DEFECT, in the corpus's own words. Several rows state the method outright — "Absence of
-- activity on this topic places her at…", "Scored based on her party", "insufficient evidence to
-- differentiate from baseline", "Assigned a moderate value". The commonest shape is an ABSENCE
-- beside an AFFILIATION: a caucus, a committee seat, an alignment or scorecard percentage, an
-- endorsement, an employer, a district, or an ideological label.
--
-- ⚠ NOT BLANKED, deliberately: rows where the absence RULES OUT A NEIGHBOURING RUNG on top of real
-- evidence (Ojeda's co-signed shelter order, Whitmer's signed AI-disclaimer law, Mayes's 303 Creative
-- statement); rows where the omission is INSIDE the person's own document and the rung is about
-- emphasis (Northcut's road-only transportation page); and scores REPORTED WITH THE RECORD BEHIND
-- THEM (Wied 33-0 with subjects named, Menéndez with every tracked vote).
--
-- ⚠ LEFT OPEN: 8 rows are sound but VINTAGE — real, on-point positions held over by "no reversal
-- documented", the oldest from 2006 and 2008, one across a party change. They are not absence
-- defects and are NOT touched here. They are a separate queue.
--
-- Applied by hand via psql; no migration runner exists in this repo, so "applied" means its data
-- effects are live. Guards below fail the whole transaction rather than write a partial result.

CREATE TEMP TABLE mig1915_decisions (
  politician_id     uuid   NOT NULL,
  topic_id          uuid   NOT NULL,
  topic_revision_id uuid   NOT NULL,
  reasoning         text   NOT NULL,
  sources           text[] NOT NULL,
  ledger_no         int    NOT NULL
) ON COMMIT DROP;

